> 
> 
> Polymorph traps are no problem, for the reason you stated; they will rip
> your cloak, if it is not a cloak of MR, but in this case it is not really
> important in the long run, as you will have a CoMR later on anyway. And
> how common are wands of death relatively to poison traps and poisoned
> orcish arrows? When I am not already poison resistant, I spend a single
> early wish on Green DSM.

That is o.k. with me.  I usually take gray DSM, and I never died from 
being poisoned after such a wish, but your point is a good one.  For me, 
getting a single wish early on means high probability of longer survival 
and therefore, I have to worry about magic resistance, since I may not 
get it easily a different way.  To lose a character to a wand of death 
or to a lich attack after 30000 turns is much worse for me than to lose 
one with gray DSM after 2000 turns due to a poison trap.  Poison 
resistance is pretty easy to get without a wish, once you have your 
unicorn horn.  Therefore, I would still go for gray DSM when I have a 
single early wish (or for Magicbane, if I have only crappy weapons).

But the thread was about how to spend one out of seven wishes.  The 
point was that one should not forget on this occasion to get poison 
resistance.  Since one of the wishes would be on some DSM other than 
green, I would then wish for a tin of green dragon meat.

> With seven wishes, I would still take the Green DSM, and add a CoMR and an
> amulet of reflection.

I like to be able to put on life saving on the astral plane or magical 
breathing on water and still have reflection.  So I would rather take 
silver DSM, CoMR and a tin of green dragon meat.

>>Also being able to have
>>reflection only by the amulet would not be desirable towards later stages of
>>the game,

> I often wear an amulet of reflection in Gehennom and on the ascension.

In nethack, I do too, except that I switch to magical breathing on water 
and to life saving when approaching Pestilence (but usually I have a 
shield then, too, which I use while not spell casting).  In slashem, you 
have to choose between wearing an amulet of reflection and one of drain 
resistance, at least if you are neutral, so it is better to get 
reflection without an amulet.

>>Moreover, since a corpse of a green dragon can give you poison resistance with
>>certainty, you don't need the scale mail at all.  Just wish for the corpse or
>>rather for a tin of it, if that works.

> It works, and you will get the poison resistance, but you give up on the
> early AC bonus (if it is a single wish).

I would not wish up poison resistance, if I had only a single wish. 
Magic resistance is more important and more difficult to get.  (And if 
you are without the amulet of reflection after Sokoban, reflection is 
more important and more difficult to get as well.)  Dying from poisoning 
may be more frequent than from wands of death, but it is still rare 
enough to take the risk to wait for an approapriate corpse.  (When 
attacked by orcs, I usually hide behind a corner, until they are close, 
so they will not shoot their arrows.  Then poisoned traps are the only 
major problem, and they are not 100% deadly anyway.)
